<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karun River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karun River is the largest river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, flowing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatt-al-arab">Shatt al-Arab</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/band-e-kaisar">Band-e Kaisar</a> dam was built across it near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shushtar">Shushtar</a>, reportedly with the labour and engineering skills of Roman prisoners. It illustrates the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>'s irrigation works.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karun-river.jpg" alt="Karun River" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shannon1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karun_river_basin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
